00:42:51.910 --> 00:42:52.310
Yeah.

1046
00:42:52.490 --> 00:42:52.650
Yeah.

1047
00:42:53.650 --> 00:42:57.750
The other one that I thought would be fun would be to be a gaffer.

1048
00:42:57.950 --> 00:42:58.870
I love light.

1049
00:42:59.810 --> 00:43:01.830
I love seeing how light changes a scene.

1050
00:43:01.970 --> 00:43:02.510
Oh, okay.

1051
00:43:02.790 --> 00:43:03.150
Yeah.

1052
00:43:03.270 --> 00:43:06.110
I mean, it's a super cool, like, artistic job.

1053
00:43:06.310 --> 00:43:11.690
Like, if there's a fakie window, you have to make me believe that's a real window using light.

1054
00:43:11.870 --> 00:43:12.230
I know.

1055
00:43:12.330 --> 00:43:14.190
And you know what else I think is so cool?

1056
00:43:14.190 --> 00:43:23.230
And we only did this a handful of times on the set of The Office, but I've done it on movies plenty of times, where you're filming and it's broad daylight,

1057
00:43:23.570 --> 00:43:26.190
but they make everything to look like nighttime.

1058
00:43:26.790 --> 00:43:27.550
Day for night.

1059
00:43:27.730 --> 00:43:28.810
They call it day for night.

1060
00:43:28.890 --> 00:43:29.050
Yeah.

1061
00:43:29.170 --> 00:43:30.790
And they black out the windows.

1062
00:43:31.190 --> 00:43:34.270
But then they'll let a little light through, like it's moonlight.

1063
00:43:34.550 --> 00:43:36.950
But you step outside and it's three o'clock in the afternoon.

1064
00:43:37.210 --> 00:43:37.390
Yeah.

1065
00:43:37.730 --> 00:43:38.490
It's so cool.

1066
00:43:38.570 --> 00:43:39.390
I couldn't do that job.

1067
00:43:39.610 --> 00:43:40.690
Lighting is really cool.

1068
00:43:40.950 --> 00:43:41.170
Yeah.

1069
00:43:41.850 --> 00:43:44.770
I don't know if I'd be good at it, but I really appreciate it.

1070
00:43:45.190 --> 00:43:45.370
Yeah.

1071
00:43:46.170 --> 00:43:47.230
Those are good answers.

1072
00:43:47.430 --> 00:43:47.590
Yeah.

1073
00:43:47.870 --> 00:43:52.510
So basically, if I wasn't acting, you think I'd be in charge of crafty?

1074
00:43:53.230 --> 00:43:53.590
Yeah.

1075
00:43:53.890 --> 00:43:54.110
Yeah.

1076
00:43:54.890 --> 00:43:59.190
And I would love to be directing, but I'm not sure it would be my strong suit.

1077
00:43:59.750 --> 00:44:01.490
So I might be line producing.

1078
00:44:01.490 --> 00:44:02.710
I might be your AD.

1079
00:44:03.050 --> 00:44:04.330
I think I'd be good at it.

1080
00:44:04.410 --> 00:44:04.730
Oh, yeah.

1081
00:44:04.810 --> 00:44:05.750
You'd be a great AD.

1082
00:44:05.910 --> 00:44:06.490
The scheduling?

1083
00:44:06.810 --> 00:44:07.110
Mm-hmm.

1084
00:44:07.290 --> 00:44:07.530
Yeah.

1085
00:44:08.410 --> 00:44:09.330
I think I would like it.

1086
00:44:09.410 --> 00:44:12.530
And if I were first AD, I'd get to be on set and I'd get to be around all the funny stuff.

1087
00:44:12.530 --> 00:44:14.810
And I'd be on set as crafty.

1088
00:44:14.950 --> 00:44:17.850
I'd be right outside the door there, but on stage.

1089
00:44:18.190 --> 00:44:20.850
Crafty is a lot of times on the stage.

1090
00:44:20.990 --> 00:44:25.390
And it's just sort of behind, like, the main structures that you're filming in.

1091
00:44:25.490 --> 00:44:27.250
So you kind of have to be quiet over there.

1092
00:44:27.370 --> 00:44:29.130
Because, you know, you've got your snacks.

1093
00:44:29.390 --> 00:44:31.270
But you see all the actors and the crew.

1094
00:44:31.850 --> 00:44:35.670
Well, if I were second AD, then I would be back there with you.

1095
00:44:35.790 --> 00:44:36.050
Yeah.

1096
00:44:36.150 --> 00:44:37.570
And then we would be best friends again.

1097
00:44:37.990 --> 00:44:38.190
Yeah.

1098
00:44:38.630 --> 00:44:38.790
Okay.

1099
00:44:38.810 --> 00:44:40.210
So you're crafty and I'm second AD.

1100
00:44:40.470 --> 00:44:40.670
Done.

1101
00:44:41.630 --> 00:44:42.530
All right, everybody.

